A second run of the port request covered the module download and
vendoring. lang/go127 is still not installed, so it used upstream's
go1.27.2 freebsd-amd64 binary as GO_CMD. With the same three distfiles
(distinfo is byte-identical to this patch's), these all completed:

- go-post-fetch, which ran "go mod download all" through the proxy
- go-post-extract, which ran "go mod tidy -e" and "go mod vendor -e"
  and wrote vendor/modules.txt. The github.com/expr-lang/expr =>
  github.com/SigNoz/expr v1.17.7-beta replace resolves.
- post-patch: every rewritten path lands in DATADIR or /var/db/signoz,
  in all four Go files and in example.yaml.

The build, stage, and plist are still not checked.

> I
> have not checked whether modernc.org/sqlite and the other dependencies
> build on every architecture, so the port has no ONLY_FOR_ARCHS yet.

The vendored modernc.org/sqlite v1.48.2 and modernc.org/libc ship
FreeBSD support only for 386, amd64, arm, and arm64, so the port cannot
build on powerpc64 or riscv64. Upstream releases only amd64 and arm64,
and the ports in the tree that set ONLY_FOR_ARCHS because of
modernc.org/sqlite list those two. I suggest:

    ONLY_FOR_ARCHS=	aarch64 amd64
    ONLY_FOR_ARCHS_REASON=	upstream only supports and releases for amd64 and arm64

portclippy, portfmt, and portlint accept this.

That run also produced a second patch for the same port before it
found this thread. I discarded it instead of posting it, so this patch
remains the only one. I left out a v2 to avoid churn before you
review. Say if you want the ONLY_FOR_ARCHS change folded into one.
